      {
        "id": 694660,
        "name": "Black Madness",
        "username": "Black_Madness",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/black_madness/{size}/410292_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-10-15T06:42:28.602Z",
        "cooked": "<p>In Eve a single player can easily hit the market, and a bunch of them can do this even worse, making any financial model useless. Provided it could ever have any usefulness …</p>\n<p>And don’t forget that CCP deployment cycle adds up a good amount of uncertainity very often.</p>\n<p>What i think could be done is a recommendation system: by analysing your clients shop list you could maybe understand “What also people could buy…” and make it available on the market. But for each system, where you want this to work, you should put up for sales lots of products, since you need that relation between item purchased and the user who bought it (which normal market data do not expose).</p>",
